 ### [Phong Shading with Shadows](4356-phong-shading-with-shadows.md)
-Phong Shading with Shadows computes the final pixel color by applying the Phong reflection model (ambient, diffuse, and specular components) to an SDF, modulated by shadow factors to simulate occlusion. It differs from its parent [Lambertian Lighting in SDF](2023-lambertian-lighting-in-sdf.md) by adding specular highlights and shadow casting, and from its sibling [Sphere Tracing with Shading](3812-sphere-tracing-with-shading.md) by explicitly separating the shading model logic from the ray-marching traversal loop, allowing for complex relighting of neural or implicit surfaces.
+Phong Shading with Shadows calculates the final color of a surface point in a Signed Distance Field (SDF) by combining ambient, diffuse, and specular lighting components defined by the Phong reflection model, modulated by shadow factors. It extends basic Lambertian shading by adding specular highlights and occlusion, allowing for the relighting of volume-rendered surfaces under directional lights. Unlike [Sphere Tracing with Shading](3812-sphere-tracing-with-shading.md), which may use simpler shading approximations, this method explicitly computes the reflection vector for specular highlights and integrates shadow rays to determine visibility.
 
